```Title: Office Application Spawning a Shell or Script Host (raw Sysmon events)```
```ATT&CK: T1204.002 | Severity: high | Sigma id: f3fb2c62-6f7e-4dae-a3f1-5bb7681ebea9```
```Data source: Sysmon EventCode 1 (Splunk Add-on for Sysmon). Change index to where your Sysmon data lives.```
```False positives: Business macros and add-ins that run commands by design (allowlist by command line)```
```Suggested ES correlation search: cron */15 * * * *, earliest=-20m@m latest=-5m@m, throttle on the table fields, notable severity high.```
index=sysmon source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
(ParentImage IN ("*\\WINWORD.EXE", "*\\EXCEL.EXE", "*\\POWERPNT.EXE", "*\\MSACCESS.EXE", "*\\MSPUB.EXE", "*\\ONENOTE.EXE") Image IN ("*\\cmd.exe", "*\\powershell.exe", "*\\pwsh.exe", "*\\wscript.exe", "*\\cscript.exe", "*\\mshta.exe", "*\\rundll32.exe", "*\\regsvr32.exe", "*\\certutil.exe", "*\\bitsadmin.exe", "*\\msbuild.exe"))
| table _time host User ParentImage Image CommandLine
